# Rank 1591 / CVE-2026-42810: Apache Polaris built its delegated
# access policies from granted storage paths used as raw string
# prefixes, so a grant on one path also authorized sibling paths
# sharing it as a text prefix -- a grant on "data" satisfied the
# startsWith conditions built for it against "data_foo/*", which
# shares the prefix but is a different object tree (policy
# prefix-match bypass, CWE-284/CWE-80). The GCS downscoping in
# polaris-core/src/main/java/org/apache/polaris/core/storage/gcp/
# GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration.java feeds
# `String path = uri.rawPath().substring(1)` from each granted
# location into two CEL condition builders:
# resourceNameStartsWithExpression formats
# "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/buckets/%s/objects/%s')"
# and objectListPrefixStartsWithExpression formats
# "api.getAttribute('storage.googleapis.com/objectListPrefix',
# '').startsWith('%s')". The fix d9731452 ("Fix GCS credential
# downscoping path traversal / prefix match bypass (#4884)") wraps
# all three extractions in StorageLocation.ensureTrailingSlash via
# a static import, so a grant on "data/" can no longer authorize
# "data_foo/*". The S3 twin of the same class of change,
# escapeIamGlobLiteral around parseS3Path(uri) and
# trimLeadingSlash(uri.rawPath()), is already present at the
# vulnerable parent in AwsCredentialsStorageIntegration.java, so
# the row's commit is the GCS delta alone.
#
# ATTENTION, policy-prefix semantics, held on recheck. The guard
# (location allowlisting) exists and runs -- its defect is that a
# string prefix is not a path segment: siblings sharing the text
# prefix match, the normalization-strength family already measured
# at ranks 1522 (bracket-blind hosts), 1582 (a wildcard pattern
# that admits every host) and 1583 (a prefix-matched URL
# allowlist). Nothing can ask "does this policy condition compare
# path segments rather than string prefixes" -- that is
# storage-policy vocabulary; of the 919 code concepts none carries
# a review condition about a compared bound needing a segment
# boundary, and the prefix-containment concepts that exist
# (CanonicalPathStringPrefixContainment, ArchiveEntryRaw
# PrefixContainment) are bound to their own applications'
# canonicalization calls. The condition literal itself is
# byte-identical at both revisions -- the fix touches only the
# value formatted into it -- so any binding keyed on the literal
# or on the format call fires 1 -> 1, and the only token-level
# difference the fix introduces is the ensureTrailingSlash wrap:
# the fix's own spelling, on a Polaris-private helper, so no
# neutraliser can name it and a Polaris binding would detect this
# platform rather than the weakness. Nor is "the value reaches the
# condition with no normaliser" a usable rule: at both revisions
# the path passes through escapeCelLiteral, a quote-and-backslash
# escaper that simply adds no boundary, so such a rule would have
# to rank one private escaper against another.
#
# Measured on the real code at the span tip (3 x --cache off per
# revision, timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB): the storage/gcp package
# reports 0 findings at d9731452^ and 0 at d9731452, stable across
# all six runs, and -flags only reports the single
# core.ResourceRelease flag on iamCredentialsClient.close
# (:266 vulnerable, :268 fixed). A full-tree scan of each revision
# (java:1452 plus python/kotlin/js/config/textpattern) reports 371
# findings, 254 at or above high, with an identical set of 183
# distinct file:line locations at both revisions -- the nearest
# storage finding is VYQL-AUTH-079 on
# stsClient.assumeRole(request.build()) in
# AwsCredentialsStorageIntegration.java:251, present unchanged at
# both. Fresh diagnosis: `vyql match` labels the parse side
# (code.XmlParse on StorageUri.parse at :325 :335 :346 vulnerable
# and :327 :341 :352 fixed) and both condition builders
# (code.FormatString on the two String.format helpers, :393 and
# :400 vulnerable), and nothing on the prefix comparison;
# `vyql resolve` reports 228 resolved / 76 unresolved where the
# unresolved set is the forEach chains and logger calls, whose
# lambda bodies still extract fully -- so no engine construct is
# mishandled and no ENGINE-GAPS.md entry is due. The generic
# candidate shape was measured rather than assumed: across the
# 286,837 java files under the rank clones (8,196,854 string
# literals), 102 literals in 26 files themselves contain
# "startsWith(", and outside this target those 17 files are HAPI
# FHIR's FHIRPath conformance expressions and their tests (50
# literals), Tomcat's jasper JSTL import scheme allowlist, Hive's
# JDO filters, OpenNMS event matchers, Graylog painless scripts
# and IoTDB/ICU test fixtures -- every one correct code or a
# fixture, so the shape buys no second true positive and still
# gives no discrimination here. No definition change shipped.
# Spec cve_rank1591 records the raw prefix grant and the
# trailing-slash form on the real file shapes, the two condition
# builders included, both asserting reject VYQL-AUTH-079: when
# policy-segment vocabulary lands, the raw prefix form must flip
# to expect.

test "rank1591: the granted path is used as a raw prefix"
  lang java
  file polaris-core/src/main/java/org/apache/polaris/core/storage/gcp/GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  import java.util.LinkedHashMap;
  import java.util.LinkedHashSet;
  import java.util.Map;
  import java.util.Set;
  import java.util.stream.Stream;

  public class GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration {
    public static CredentialAccessBoundary generateAccessBoundaryRules(
        Set<String> allowedReadLocations, Set<String> allowedListLocations) {
      Map<String, LinkedHashSet<String>> readConditionsByBucket = new LinkedHashMap<>();

      Stream.concat(allowedReadLocations.stream(), allowedListLocations.stream())
          .distinct()
          .forEach(
              location -> {
                StorageUri uri = StorageUri.parse(location);
                String bucket = uri.authority();
                String path = uri.rawPath().substring(1);
                readConditionsByBucket
                    .computeIfAbsent(bucket, key -> new LinkedHashSet<>())
                    .add(resourceNameStartsWithExpression(bucket, path));
              });

      allowedListLocations.forEach(
          location -> {
            StorageUri uri = StorageUri.parse(location);
            String bucket = uri.authority();
            String path = uri.rawPath().substring(1);
            readConditionsByBucket
                .computeIfAbsent(bucket, key -> new LinkedHashSet<>())
                .add(objectListPrefixStartsWithExpression(path));
          });

      return accessBoundary(readConditionsByBucket);
    }

    static String resourceNameStartsWithExpression(String bucket, String path) {
      return String.format(
          "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/buckets/%s/objects/%s')",
          escapeCelLiteral(bucket), escapeCelLiteral(path));
    }

    static String objectListPrefixStartsWithExpression(String path) {
      return String.format(
          "api.getAttribute('storage.googleapis.com/objectListPrefix', '').startsWith('%s')",
          escapeCelLiteral(path));
    }

    static String escapeCelLiteral(String value) {
      return value.replace("'", "\\'");
    }

    static CredentialAccessBoundary accessBoundary(
        Map<String, LinkedHashSet<String>> conditionsByBucket) {
      CredentialAccessBoundary.Builder builder = CredentialAccessBoundary.newBuilder();
      conditionsByBucket.forEach(
          (bucket, conditions) ->
              builder.addRule(
                  CredentialAccessBoundary.AccessBoundaryRule.newBuilder()
                      .setAvailabilityExpression(String.join(" || ", conditions))
                      .build()));
      return builder.build();
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1591: the fixed revision forces a segment boundary"
  lang java
  file polaris-core/src/main/java/org/apache/polaris/core/storage/gcp/GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  import static org.apache.polaris.core.storage.StorageLocation.ensureTrailingSlash;

  import java.util.LinkedHashMap;
  import java.util.LinkedHashSet;
  import java.util.Map;
  import java.util.Set;
  import java.util.stream.Stream;

  public class GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration {
    public static CredentialAccessBoundary generateAccessBoundaryRules(
        Set<String> allowedReadLocations, Set<String> allowedListLocations) {
      Map<String, LinkedHashSet<String>> readConditionsByBucket = new LinkedHashMap<>();

      Stream.concat(allowedReadLocations.stream(), allowedListLocations.stream())
          .distinct()
          .forEach(
              location -> {
                StorageUri uri = StorageUri.parse(location);
                String bucket = uri.authority();
                // Treat the granted path as a directory prefix: a trailing slash is required so
                // that the downstream startsWith() CEL conditions cannot be satisfied by sibling
                // objects or list prefixes that merely share the granted path as a string prefix
                // (e.g. a grant on "data/" must not authorize access to "data_foo/*)".
                String path = ensureTrailingSlash(uri.rawPath().substring(1));
                readConditionsByBucket
                    .computeIfAbsent(bucket, key -> new LinkedHashSet<>())
                    .add(resourceNameStartsWithExpression(bucket, path));
              });

      allowedListLocations.forEach(
          location -> {
            StorageUri uri = StorageUri.parse(location);
            String bucket = uri.authority();
            String path = ensureTrailingSlash(uri.rawPath().substring(1));
            readConditionsByBucket
                .computeIfAbsent(bucket, key -> new LinkedHashSet<>())
                .add(objectListPrefixStartsWithExpression(path));
          });

      return accessBoundary(readConditionsByBucket);
    }

    static String resourceNameStartsWithExpression(String bucket, String path) {
      return String.format(
          "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/buckets/%s/objects/%s')",
          escapeCelLiteral(bucket), escapeCelLiteral(path));
    }

    static String objectListPrefixStartsWithExpression(String path) {
      return String.format(
          "api.getAttribute('storage.googleapis.com/objectListPrefix', '').startsWith('%s')",
          escapeCelLiteral(path));
    }

    static String escapeCelLiteral(String value) {
      return value.replace("'", "\\'");
    }

    static CredentialAccessBoundary accessBoundary(
        Map<String, LinkedHashSet<String>> conditionsByBucket) {
      CredentialAccessBoundary.Builder builder = CredentialAccessBoundary.newBuilder();
      conditionsByBucket.forEach(
          (bucket, conditions) ->
              builder.addRule(
                  CredentialAccessBoundary.AccessBoundaryRule.newBuilder()
                      .setAvailabilityExpression(String.join(" || ", conditions))
                      .build()));
      return builder.build();
    }
  }
  ```
